comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T18:53:40.315Z",codex-agent,Implementation and real-repository regression evidence linked. Review remains with the orchestrator; this item stays in progress.
  "2026-10-15T19:02:34.909Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: replaced only cleanOrder with input order. The real three-lane ordering regression failed with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. All six permutations are checked; only a then b then c is clean. Restored exact function bytes. Linked tests are checked on every merged candidate before local execution."
  "2026-10-15T19:35:48.173Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: investigate hosted-ref trust semantics, test explicit refused and acknowledged states, and return the largest deterministic clean landing order with blocked-peer diagnostics. Preserve nonzero partial-land exit."
  "2026-10-15T19:39:21.558Z",codex-agent,"Root cause confirmed in pinned SDK: GITHUB_HEAD_REF/GITHUB_REF_NAME override local Git branch for provenance and trust; CI=true alone grants nothing. Reproduced original untrusted assertion failure with matching hosted ref under isolated HOME/Git config. Tests now isolate source-workspace and hosted refs and separately verify foreign refusal, explicit acknowledgement, and host-contract matching-ref execution."
  "2026-10-15T19:40:50.915Z",codex-agent,"Candidate-tree regression exposed another inherited-environment issue: the verification subprocess inherited PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT from the parent PM run and could snapshot the parent checkout instead of the simulated merge. Bind the child source workspace to the verification worktree. The existing merged-source assertion detects this behavior."
  "2026-10-15T19:43:56.082Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only the pre-round landLanes implementation (plus its original import) makes partial-land regression fail, exit 1: order [] instead of the expected two-lane clean subset. Restoring only inherited child source-workspace behavior makes the existing merged-source regression fail with Linked tests failed, exit 1. Both changes restored exactly. Trust fixture reversion under CI=true/GITHUB_ACTIONS=true with hosted PR ref fails provenance assertion (hosted ref instead of authoring), exit 1; original /untrusted/ refusal assertion remains intact. Baseline original test also reproduced the runner command-execution failure."
  "2026-10-15T19:51:46.272Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 PM-linked acceptance: pm test pm-swarm-jt6d --run --progress passed 2 linked command(s), 17 tests, zero failures. Full post-run snapshots unchanged: two registered worktrees, zero parallel branches, zero swarm Git configuration keys. Source, tracker and settings mutations remained inside scratch repositories."
  "2026-10-15T20:04:14.574Z",codex-agent,"Additional runner-version validation: CI-like hosted-ref trust regressions pass 2/2 on Node 22.23.1 and 2/2 on Node 26.7.0. Real CLI partial execution returns exit 1, merges the clean selected subset and preserves the blocked ref and worktree. Greedy-prefix regression confirms largest-subset search and deterministic ordering."
